  <div id="sutta">
  
              <h2 id="SN2.19" class="h1">Uttara the Deva’s Son<br/>
                Uttara Sutta  (SN 2:19)</h2>
              <p>Near Rājagaha. As he was standing to one side, Uttara the deva’s son recited this verse in the Blessed One’s presence:</p>
              <div class="verse">
                <p>“Life is swept along,</p>
                <p>next-to-nothing its span.</p>
                <p>For one swept on by aging</p>
                <p class="v1">no shelters exist.</p>
                <p>Perceiving this danger in death,</p>
                <p>one should do deeds of merit</p>
                <p class="v1">that bring about bliss.”</p>
                <div class="verse-add">
                  <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                  <p>“Life is swept along,</p>
                  <p>next-to-nothing its span.</p>
                  <p>For one swept to old age</p>
                  <p class="v1">no shelters exist.</p>
                  <p>Perceiving this danger in death,</p>
                  <p>one should drop the world’s bait</p>
                  <p class="v1">and look for peace.”</p>
                </div>
              </div>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
